Third-party / derived components
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1) ps5-payload-websrv BigApp loader (GPL-3.0-or-later)
   Author: John Törnblom
   Used in: prospero_media_standalone/core/ (hbldr, elfldr, pt)
   Upstream: https://github.com/ps5-payload-dev/websrv
   (and related ps5-payload projects)

   These modules implement the system BigApp host prepare + ELF replace
   path. They remain under GPL-3.0-or-later. ProsperoPlayer packaging
   adapted them for Prospero title IDs and the Prospero media launcher.

2) FFmpeg libraries (linked via PS5 homebrew SDK builds)
   Used for demux/decode/resample/scale in the player.
   FFmpeg is typically LGPL/GPL depending on how it was configured.
   Your SDK’s libav* binaries determine the exact FFmpeg license terms;
   check your SDK / FFmpeg build documentation when redistributing.

3) Sony PlayStation 5 system libraries (Sce*)
   Proprietary. Linked only as system APIs on a jailbroken console.
   Not redistributed as source in this repository.

4) Mozilla CA root store (MPL-2.0)
   Used in: addons/src/evo_ca_bundle.c, generated at build time by
   tools/gen_ca_bundle.py from the build image's ca-certificates bundle.
   The roots evo_net trusts for verified TLS (the Twitch login).
   Licence text and where to get the source: assets/licenses/ca-certificates.txt

5) qrcodegen 1.8.0 (MIT)
   Author: Project Nayuki
   Used in: ../../../core/third_party/qrcodegen (the QR code on the Twitch
   login screen)
   Upstream: https://github.com/nayuki/QR-Code-generator
   Vendored with one change: no <sstream>, to match the PS5 app's build.
   Licence text: assets/licenses/qrcodegen.txt

6) Fonts, built into the app (eboot.bin)
   Lato (LatoLatin) - SIL Open Font License 1.1
     the RmlUi screens; licence text: assets/fonts/Lato-OFL.txt
   Inter and Montserrat - SIL Open Font License 1.1
     the kit screens; licence texts: assets/hui/fonts/Inter-LICENSE.txt,
     assets/hui/fonts/Montserrat-LICENSE.txt
   DejaVu Sans Mono - Bitstream Vera License (DejaVu changes public domain)
     the kit's monospaced figures; licence text:
     assets/hui/fonts/DejaVu-LICENSE.txt

7) Lucide icons (ISC; the icons derived from Feather are MIT)
   Author: Lucide Icons and Contributors; Feather: Cole Bemis
   Used in: the app's line icons (assets/icons, built into eboot.bin)
   Upstream: https://github.com/lucide-icons/lucide
   Licence text: assets/licenses/lucide.txt

